1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,400
A coil opposes AC with its reactance, XL.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,900
XL grows with the frequency f.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,300
At 50 Hz the coil has a certain XL.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,400
At 60 Hz it is 20 % larger.

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,900
The same voltage then drives about 17 % less current.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:28,000
Shore power is often 50 Hz. Ships often run 60 Hz.

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:33,900
Coils, motors and transformers are built for one frequency. Check the plate.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,900
Frequency matters. Every time.
